    "summary": "Get All Credit Usage",
    "deprecated": false,
    "description": "Read operation. Retrieve all required pages before reporting complete totals. Returns a paginated list of credit usage records for the account. A credit usage records that a client consumed an amount of a given credit type (the counterpart of a credit charge).\n\nThis is a v2 native-entity endpoint served from the `/v2/api/entity` base and authenticated with a Bearer token.\n\nThe trailing path segment (`1`) is the **data level** — how deeply related records are loaded — not a page number. `/credit_usage/list` and `/credit_usage/list/1` return the same result. Pagination is controlled by the `page` and `per_page` query parameters.\n\n| Parameter | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `page` | Page number (default `1`). |\n| `per_page` | Items per page (default `20`). |\n| `filter[<field>][<operator>]` | Filter rows by a field's value, e.g. `filter[client_id][equal]=8`. |\n| `sort[<field>]` | Sort by a field, `asc` or `desc`, e.g. `sort[usage_date]=desc`. |\n\n**Filterable fields.** The fields intended for filtering:\n\n| Field | Type | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| `client_id` | integer (client) | `filter[client_id][equal]=8` |\n| `credit_type_id` | integer (credit type) | `filter[credit_type_id][equal]=1` |\n| `usage_date` | date | `filter[usage_date][greater_than_equal]=2025-01-01` |\n\nThe list will in fact filter and sort on any existing column, not only the fields above. When no `sort` is given the default ordering is newest first (`id` descending).\n\nEach item in `data` is a flat credit-usage record.",
    "tags": [
      "Endpoints/Points & Credits/Credit Usage"
    ],
